===Etymology===
From {{w|Anglo-Frisian}} ''*feuwær'' [ˈfeu̯.wær], from {{w|West Germanic}} ''*feuwar'' [ˈfeu̯.wɑr], from ''*fewwār'' [ˈfeu̯.wɑːr], from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*fedwōr}} [ˈɸeð.woːr], from ''*petwṓr'', from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*kʷetwóres}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|fiūwer}} ({{cog|fy|fjouwer}}), {{cog|osx|fiuwar}} ({{cog|nds|veer}}), {{cog|odt|*fiuwar}} ({{cog|nl|vier}}), {{cog|goh|fior}} ({{cog|de|vier}}), {{cog|non|fjórir}} ({{cog|sv|fyra}}), {{cog|got|𐍆𐌹𐌳𐍅𐍉𐍂}}. Indo-European cognates include {{cog|sla-pro|*četyre}}, {{cog|sga|cethair}}, {{cog|grc|τέσσαρες}}, {{cog|la|quattuor}}.

